{"id": "EUVD-2026-102492", "enisaUuid": "18a2fb1e-b765-3beb-bf13-8420d1fbb7ab", "description": "Likeshop through 3.5.1 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in AfterSale.php and AfterSaleLogic.php that lets authenticated users access other customers' after-sale records by supplying their ids. Attackers with self-registered accounts can call the detail, goodsInfo, cancel, express, and again actions to read refund and order data, cancel refunds, overwrite return shipment details, or re-open refused refunds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:46:15", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/likeshop-after-sale-api-cross-user-idor", "https://github.com/likeadmin-likeshop/likeshop/blob/3.5.1/server/application/api/controller/AfterSale.php#L52-L102", "https://github.com/likeadmin-likeshop/likeshop/blob/3.5.1/server/application/api/logic/AfterSaleLogic.php#L251-L377", "https://github.com/likeadmin-likeshop/likeshop", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/likeshop-through-3.5.1-idor-via-aftersale-api-refund-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111348", "GHSA-5vm9-2pq9-4q7r"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7fa5f96d-4f98-3b36-96f2-2a49c626d083", "product": {"name": "Likeshop", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.5.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "05797acb-0a62-3e81-8b42-b0dd48f156d2", "vendor": {"name": "likeshop"}}], "isExploited": false}